y reports and expert estimates frequently characterize it as a **~10 trillion parameter model**[1][2][3].\n\nKey details regarding its scale and architecture include:\n\n*   **Estimated Scale:** Most industry analysis and reports place the total parameter count at approximately **8 to 10 trillion**[4][1][5][6]. \n*   **Mixture of Experts (MoE):** It is widely believed that Mythos utilizes a **Mixture of Experts (MoE)** architecture[7][2][6]. This allows the model to possess a massive \"knowledge capacity\" while maintaining greater computational efficiency, as only a fraction of its total parameters are active during any single forward pass[2][6]. \n*   **Active Parameters:** While the total parameter count is estimated at 10 trillion, researchers have suggested that the number of active parameters per token is significantly lower—likely in the range of **800 billion to 1.2 trillion**—to manage inference latency and compute requirements[2].\n*   **Comparison:** For context, this scale represents a significant leap from previous generations of frontier models, such as Claude Opus (often estimated in the 1–2 trillion range)[7][3].\n\nBecause Anthropic maintains the model as a proprietary, restricted-access system (often deployed through programs like Project Glasswing), these figures remain based on independent estimates and leaked information rather than official technical specifications[4][8][9].\n\nSources:\n[1] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHOD-4FV6GtknnDrLA8cf1HvwHMMzMood3eWMeQFFqqrZLtmhrgVtXr651hYNWOk3c-_KIcnG15_FnVq1UnAZCXBhyc-Qmdeki0SMqYYV0xMqGQBiBrIWbLMUpWlqIkN1QDQUsOglgyOOvtAx7WMtywnQlDFovOPa_Bx_cu14XEChbFQf82gpd6kb0Pk16qfmVTBBksNPtW2jlxuPJI52Up5aV0C8mCSZhGatOAK-JlU4DHxYA1SBTgvX7jQ9EndevK_g\n<truncated 94 bytes>\npZoaovrxx0ObVMT0WX2R_6PL3pBveyVgKTMfBIstVCvocXdXX_IHO5j7s-zUSnLLWWoQ9IRXn1FwsJ8DBkE7SgiQsd4_N7o3z7mp0HLlVwG9Q1kFF8LvxfeR2lwyUeue9Fp1VHk0E_i8hmjkZsrp1maHAWJ3YF6vwDCGgS1B04DknrTVrABjVt_PzHC9EPIr)\n[3